.SH DESCRIPTION
Converts a signal name string to its numeric signal number.
Accepts three input formats:
.IP "1." 3
\f[B]Full name\f[R]: \f[CR]\(dqSIGINT\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqSIGTERM\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqSIGKILL\(dq\f[R], etc.
.IP "2." 3
\f[B]Short name\f[R]: \f[CR]\(dqINT\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dqTERM\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dqKILL\(dq\f[R], etc.
(the \f[CR]SIG\f[R] prefix is stripped automatically).
.IP "3." 3
\f[B]Numeric string\f[R]: \f[CR]\(dq2\(dq\f[R], \f[CR]\(dq9\(dq\f[R],
\f[CR]\(dq15\(dq\f[R], etc.
(converted via \f[CR]atoi()\f[R]).
